    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2XiKyj2vtZdjMMhEXcKPktV)_\n\n## Merge order\n- Base: `main`, which already contains #463 (merged).\n- Touches only `sp-pdf-reader` (`.el` and its literate `.org`).\n- Independent of every open PR.\n\n## What\n- Problem: `M-x emureader-build` fails with `gmake: *** No rule to make target 'module'` in `var/elpaca/builds/emureader/`.\n- Cause (checked on the checkout on Sia's Mac):\n  - `emureader-build` runs `gmake module` in `emureader-directory`, the directory of the loaded `emureader.el`, which is the Elpaca builds dir.\n  - Elpaca's default `:files` links only `*.el` and a few docs there, so there is no `Makefile` and no `render/*.c`.\n  - The `Makefile` and sources are in `var/elpaca/sources/emureader/`; running `gmake module` there works on macOS (it is not a macOS problem).\n  - Elpaca also deletes and recreates the builds dir on every build, so a module built there would be lost.\n- Fix, in the `use-package` recipe:\n  - `:build (:before elpaca-build-link sp-pdf-reader--elpaca-build-module)`: runs `gmake module` in the source dir before linking.\n    - A failure (e.g. MuPDF missing) is only printed in the Elpaca log, so `lsp-mode` and other dependants still build.\n  - `:files (:defaults \"Makefile\" \"render\" \"emureader-dyn.*\")`: links the module, `Makefile` and `render/` into the builds dir, where `emureader` looks for the module.\n    - `M-x emureader-build` also works as a manual fallback.\n- Literate doc updated as bullet lists.\n\n## Not verified\n- The `:build` step and the `:files` linking have not run end to end (cloud container has no Elpaca/Emacs setup of Sia's).\n- `elpaca-defscript` is used through `eval` because it is a macro that only exists under Elpaca.\n\n## Manual testing\n- [ ] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 464-emureader-module-build; git checkout 464-emureader-module-build`, restart Emacs.\n- [ ] `M-x elpaca-rebuild RET emureader`; the `*elpaca-log*` shows `sp-pdf-reader--elpaca-build-module` running `gmake module` with no failure message.\n- [ ] `ls -l ~/.config/emacs-modular/var/elpaca/builds/emureader/` shows `Makefile`, `render` and `emureader-dyn.dylib` links.\n- [ ] Restart Emacs; `M-: (progn (require 'emureader) (featurep 'emureader-dyn))` after opening a PDF, or `M-: (sp-pdf-reader-ready-p)` → `t`.\n- [ ] `M-x emureader-build` in the new setup finishes with `Compilation finished` (manual fallback).\n- [ ] `M-: (list (fboundp 'emureader-open-doc) (fboundp 'emureader-goto-page))` → `(t t)`.\n- [ ] `M-x sp-pdf-open` on a PDF opens it in emureader; `C-u` and page 5 opens at page 5.\n- [ ] Optional: with `mupdf` temporarily unlinked, `elpaca-rebuild` still finishes and the log shows the \"module build failed\" hint.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBWtETz7fdpswkRh5P)_",
